    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 35 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection (409) of a create-owner request whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness feature.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckEmailUnique.java` \u2014 reads the (already lower-cased) email from the validated `OwnerFieldsDto`, skips when absent/blank (email is optional), and throws `DuplicateEmailException` if any existing owner has a case-insensitively matching email.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the telephone handler.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkEmailUnique` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the uniqueness read runs in the same write transaction as the insert) between `checkTelephoneUnique` and `checkHouseholdUnique`.\n\nThe Cp25 acceptance test (`email-unique`) passes, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
